  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ASEAN-region Preventive Diplomacy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Two regional workshops on maritime security and preventive diplomacy for the region soon to be run by The Asia Foundation. In alignment with State Department&apos;s support for fostering constructive engagement with and between member countries of the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN), The Asia Foundation will convene two substantive regional dialogue forums to discuss two issues of particular significance to the region and to U.S. foreign policy priorities: maritime security and the disaster management capacity of the ASEAN region. To be held in in Kuala Lumpur and Bangkok, respectively, these forums will serve as venues for senior government officials and distinguished specialists from think tanks, academia, and civil society institutions to discuss, debate, and provide recommendations on the regional dimensions of critical issues facing the ASEAN community. As a resource for future discussion and policy development, conference reports will be issued after each forum, which will present the substantive recommendations emerging from the discussions.</narrative>
  </description>
